  "description": "The full Open API sequence: client_credentials token exchange, site list, then devices and clients for the one site. Proves the non-standard 'Authorization: AccessToken=<token>' header is sent, that the {errorCode, msg, result} envelope is unwrapped, that hyphenated uppercase MACs are canonicalised, and that a device named after its own MAC does not get that MAC as a hostname. Envelope and token shapes follow a real capture of an Omada software controller; the device field set follows a capture from an OC200 on firmware 5.13.30.20.",

